cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "NOT PINNs: a controlled comparison of soft and hard physics constraints in neural dynamics models"
message: "If you use this benchmark or its findings, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Sarra
    alias: eigenthingy
abstract: >-
  A controlled study of four ways to impose a conservation law on a neural
  vector-field model: no constraint, a soft loss penalty on the energy
  residual, a Hamiltonian architecture that exactly conserves a learned
  invariant, and a projection architecture that exactly conserves the known
  physical energy. All four are trained on identical noisy data with matched
  parameter counts and identical optimizer budgets, and scored on accuracy,
  long-horizon stability, extrapolation to unseen energy shells, observation
  noise, data efficiency, and model misspecification. 560 runs over three
  systems (nonlinear pendulum, Henon-Heiles, damped pendulum) with five seeds
  and bootstrap confidence intervals.
keywords:
  - physics-informed neural networks
  - Hamiltonian neural networks
  - scientific machine learning
  - conservation laws
  - benchmark
  - neural ODE
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-08-14
